[center][size=6][b][color=#f4a261]✨ OStim Prism[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][b]The Modern, Customizable Magelight UI Overhaul for OStim Standalone[/b][/size]
[size=2][color=#aaaaaa]Full Mouse & Controller Support  •  Drag & Drop HUD  •  Icon Grid or List  •  3D Actor Portraits[/color][/size][/center]

[line]

[b]OStim Prism[/b] replaces the default OStim interface with a sleek, responsive overlay powered by [b]Magelight UI[/b]. Control scenes with your mouse, keyboard, or controller—customize every panel's position and size right on screen, switch between a compact icon grid or classic list, and track every participant's stats at a glance.

[quote][b][color=#64b5f6]⚡ Now Powered by Magelight UI (v2.0.0)[/color][/b]
OStim Prism has migrated from Prisma UI to [b]Magelight UI[/b] for smoother rendering, zero performance cost when hidden, native gamepad navigation, and seamless focus switching with other Magelight overlays like [b]OStim Navigator[/b].[/quote]

[line]

[size=5][color=#f4a261][b]🚀 Key Features[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*][b]🖱️ Full Cursor & Gamepad Support:[/b] Toggle the mouse cursor anytime (default [b]Left Alt[/b]) to click menus directly, or navigate with your controller.[/*]
[*][b]🔲 Classic Icon Grid or List Menu:[/b] Switch between a clean classic icon grid (with customizable columns × rows and a bottom label bar) or vertical list—anytime from the HUD toolbar.[/*]
[*][b]📐 Drag-and-Drop Positioning & Scaling:[/b] Move the main menu panel and the excitement circles anywhere on screen and scale each block from [b]30% to 250%[/b]. Your layout is saved automatically and carries over between saves.[/*]
[*][b]🖼️ 3D Actor Portraits:[/b] When [b][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/197470][/url][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/197470][/url][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/197470]Phantasm 1.2+[/url][/b] is installed, excitement circles can show live 3D portraits of every actor in the scene with their climax counter below—or toggle portraits off for the classic counter.[/*]
[*][b]🧬 Complete Actor Tracking:[/b] Track excitement, [b]OEndurance[/b] (stamina), and [b]OCum[/b] (cum storage) for [i]every[/i] actor in the scene, color-coded by sex: [color=#1e90ff][b]Male[/b][/color] • [color=#ff69b4][b]Female[/b][/color] • [color=#9370db][b]Other[/b][/color].[/*]
[*][b]🔍 Smart Search & Precision Alignment:[/b] Find scenes by name or ID with [b]Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V[/b] paste support, and type exact coordinates or rotation values instead of tapping keys.[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#f4a261][b]🎮 Quick-Start Guide[/b][/color][/size]

[size=3][b][color=#64b5f6]1. Switching Between Game & UI Focus[/color][/b][/size]
Press [b]Left Alt[/b] (customizable in [font=Courier New]OStimPrism.ini[/font]) at any time during a scene to toggle UI Focus:
[list]
[*][b]Unfocused (Game Mode):[/b] Standard OStim Standalone keyboard controls.[/*]
[*][b]Focused (Cursor Mode):[/b] A cursor appears and your mouse, keyboard, and controller inputs go directly to OStim Prism so you can click buttons, scroll, or type in Search without triggering Skyrim hotkeys.[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][b][color=#64b5f6]2. Customizing Your Layout (Drag, Scale, Grid, Portraits)[/color][/b][/size]
No config file editing required! Enter [b]Cursor Mode[/b] ([b]Left Alt[/b]) and hover your mouse over either the [b]Main Panel[/b] or the [b]Excitement Circles[/b] to reveal its layout toolbar:
[list]
[*][b]Move:[/b] Grab the [b]4-way drag handle[/b] and drop the panel anywhere on your screen.[/*]
[*][b]Resize:[/b] Click [b]−[/b] / [b]+[/b] or click the percentage box to type a scale between [b]30%[/b] and [b]250%[/b].[/*]
[*][b]Grid vs. List (Main Panel):[/b] Click the [b]Grid / List[/b] toggle button to switch menu styles. When Grid mode is active, set your preferred [b]Cols × Rows[/b] (1–12) right next to it.[/*]
[*][b]Portraits vs. No Portraits (Excitement Circles):[/b] Click the [b]Portraits / No Portraits[/b] toggle button to show or hide 3D actor portraits inside the excitement rings.[/*]
[/list]
Every change is saved automatically to [font=Courier New]OStimPrism.ini[/font] so it persists across reloads and new saves.

[size=3][b][color=#64b5f6]3. Navigating Menus with Keyboard or Controller[/color][/b][/size]
OStim Prism keeps OStim's familiar controls and splits the main panel into two areas:
[list]
[*][b]The Sidebar (Left Buttons):[/b] Switch between [i]Navigation[/i], [i]Options[/i], [i]Search[/i], and [i]Align[/i].
[list]
[*][b]Up / Down:[/b] Cycle through buttons.[/*]
[*][b]Enter / Yes:[/b] Open the highlighted menu.[/*]
[*][b]Right:[/b] Move focus into the active menu.[/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[*][b]The Menu Area (Right Content):[/b] Browse scenes, options, search, or alignment.
[list]
[*][b]Left:[/b] Return to the Sidebar (from [i]Navigation[/i] or [i]Options[/i]).[/*]
[*][b]Tab / Esc:[/b] Return to the Sidebar from [i]Search[/i] or [i]Align[/i] (since Left/Right are used for typing and adjusting values).[/*]
[*][b]Mouse Wheel:[/b] Scroll through lists or grids smoothly without hovering causing auto-scroll jumps.[/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#f4a261][b]📊 Widgets at a Glance[/b][/color][/size]

[list]
[*][b]✨ Precision Alignment:[/b] Click any coordinate or rotation box in the Align menu to type an exact number, or use [b]Up / Down[/b] to pick an attribute and hold [b]Left / Right[/b] for fast adjustment.[/*]
[*][b]🔍 Smart Search:[/b] Instantly filter scenes by name or ID, with full [b]Ctrl+C / Ctrl+V[/b] support.[/*]
[*][b]⚙️ Thread Status Ring:[/b] Shows current animation speed in the center, speed segments around the ring, and icons for Auto-Mode, Manual Mode, and Control Locks.[/*]
[*][b]🧬 Excitement Circles:[/b] One ring per actor displaying [b]Excitement[/b] (inner ring), [b]Stamina / OEndurance[/b] (outer left), [b]Cum / OCum[/b] (outer right), and either a [b]3D Portrait[/b] or [b]Climax Counter[/b] in the center.[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#f4a261][b]⚙️ Configuration (OStimPrism.ini)[/b][/color][/size]
Most layout options can be changed directly in-game using the hover toolbars, which update [font=Courier New]Data\SKSE\Plugins\OStimPrism.ini[/font] automatically. You can also edit it manually for extra options:

[list]
[*][b][Hotkeys][/b] (uses standard Skyrim DXScanCodes)
[list]
[*][b]ToggleFocus:[/b] Key to toggle UI Focus / cursor mode (Default: [i]56[/i] / Left Alt).[/*]
[*][b]ToggleInspector:[/b] Key to open the WebUI developer inspector (Default: [i]157[/i] / Right Ctrl).[/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[*][b][UIBehaviour][/b]
[list]
[*][b]EnableGridMenu:[/b] [i]1[/i] for Icon Grid, [i]0[/i] for classic Vertical List (also toggleable in-game).[/*]
[*][b]GridColumns / GridRows:[/b] Grid size from [i]1[/i] to [i]12[/i] (Default: [i]4 × 4[/i], also editable in-game).[/*]
[*][b]MainBlockX / MainBlockY / MainBlockScale:[/b] Saved position and scale (%) of the main panel.[/*]
[*][b]ExcitementBlockX / ExcitementBlockY / ExcitementBlockScale:[/b] Saved position and scale (%) of the excitement circles.[/*]
[*][b]EnablePortraits:[/b] [i]1[/i] to show 3D Phantasm portraits, [i]0[/i] for classic climax counters (also toggleable in-game).[/*]
[*][b]IdleTimeoutSeconds:[/b] Seconds of inactivity before the HUD auto-hides. Set to [i]0[/i] to keep it visible at all times (Default: [i]30[/i]).[/*]
[*][b]TrackedMenus:[/b] Comma-separated list of Skyrim menus (Inventory, Map, Console, etc.) that automatically hide OStim Prism when opened. Add custom mod menu names here if needed.[/*]
[/list]
[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][color=#f4a261][b]❓ FAQ[/b][/color][/size]

[quote][b]The UI is too big, too small, or in the wrong spot.[/b]
Press [b]Left Alt[/b] and hover over the panel you want to adjust. Use the toolbar that appears to drag it anywhere on screen and change its scale from 30% to 250%.[/quote]

[quote][b]Why aren't 3D portraits showing up in the excitement circles?[/b]
3D portraits require [b]Phantasm[/b] to be installed and [b]Portraits[/b] enabled on the excitement circles' layout toolbar. If Phantasm isn't installed, the circles automatically show the classic climax counter instead.[/quote]

[quote][b]A Skyrim message box popped up while I was in Cursor Mode and I can't click it.[/b]
Press [b]Left Alt[/b] to exit Cursor Mode, handle the Skyrim popup, then press [b]Left Alt[/b] again to return to OStim Prism.[/quote]

[quote][b]A custom HUD or menu from another mod overlaps with OStim Prism.[/b]
Add that menu's internal name to [font=Courier New]TrackedMenus[/font] in [font=Courier New]OStimPrism.ini[/font] so OStim Prism hides automatically while it's open.[/quote]

[line]

[size=5][color=#f4a261][b]🐞 Filing Issues & Bug Reports[/b][/color][/size]
If something breaks or looks off, please share:
[list=1]
[*][b]Log files[/b] from [i]Documents\My Games\Skyrim Special Edition\SKSE[/i]: [font=Courier New]OStimPrism.log[/font], [font=Courier New]Magelight.log[/font], [font=Courier New]OStim.log[/font], and your latest Crash Log (if you CTD'd).[/*]
[*][b]Mod context:[/b] Relevant OStim/UI addons you use (e.g., Phantasm, OCum, OEndurance, OStim Navigator).[/*]
[*][b]Steps to reproduce:[/b] What you were doing right before the issue happened.[/*]
[/list]

